# Credentials — never commit these
# .env, .env.local, ".env copy.example" — any variant may hold real secrets;
# the committed template (.env.example) is re-included below.
.env*
!.env.example
Neo4j-*.txt

# Local Claude settings (machine-local paths / personal permission rules)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Node (web/)
node_modules/

# ADK local runtime state (agents/ — session DBs the api_server writes)
.adk/

# Test / type / lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Sample / local data — may contain sensitive source data
drydocs/data/
# Staging / extract output (real data — keep local, never commit)
stg_out/
/stg_*/

# SDLC-Docs — employer-internal source corpus (the SDLC process docs the extracted
# design artifacts were distilled from): keep LOCAL for reference, never commit/publish.
# Internal, confidential material per PUBLISH-BOUNDARY.md — the raw files carry the
# employer's real name, internal URLs, and internal tool/standard code names (which is
# exactly why the comment here names none of them; J27). Ignore the WHOLE corpus
# (docx/doc/pdf/xls/txt/json, any type) and keep only the clean design artifacts
# SDLC-Docs/extracted/*.md tracked.
/SDLC-Docs/*
!/SDLC-Docs/extracted/
/SDLC-Docs/extracted/*
!/SDLC-Docs/extracted/*.md

# Local doc-extraction helper scripts (temporary; generated the SDLC-Docs corpus)
/.tmp_*

# Oracle Kerberos connection — the FILLED config holds a real SID/hosts/alias.
# Only the .sample.txt is committed.
libs/oracle_kerberos/oracle_kerberos_connection.txt

# Local real-data working area (Internal, confidential material): consolidated
# troubleshooting notes, screenshots with live values, filled configs.
# Never committed; travels to the company side by hand, not by git.
/internal-local/

# Raw screenshots/images dropped in the REPO ROOT during troubleshooting/porting —
# they routinely contain live SIDs, hostnames, EPV objects, ADFS client IDs.
# Blanket rule: no root-level images are ever committed (verified: none tracked).
# Committed images live in purposeful homes (drydocs-icons/, docs/). Move drops
# into internal-local/ when done; this is the safety net.
/*.png
/*.webp
/*.svg
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# Books / reports dropped in the REPO ROOT (e.g. Essential-GraphRAG.pdf — publicly
# available Manning/Neo4j ebook, cite by URL; annual-report inputs). Publisher PDFs
# are never committed (copyright + repo size); the registration lives in
# reference/research/README.md. Tracked PDFs live in purposeful homes (docs/design/ui-exploration/).
/*.pdf

# Third-party design template source (O21, 2026-07-21) — the Keenthemes
# "Start React Free" Figma file is a VENDOR ASSET (19 MB); committing it here
# would redistribute it on a sometimes-published repo (license unverifiable
# offline — same rule as the vendor PDFs below). Our own extraction from it
# (layout-anatomy-checklist.md, structure only, no code copied) IS committed.
docs/design/ui-exploration/start-react-free-reference.fig

# Vendor PDF posters/manuals — copyrighted BMC (and other vendor) binaries kept
# as LOCAL reference only. This repo is sometimes published; the *.md files in
# external/orchestration/ are our own summaries and are publishable, the raw
# vendor PDFs are not. Facts from the poster are transcribed in the controlm-db
# skill (references/er-model.md).
external/orchestration/**/*.pdf

# ServiceNow doc set (C10, 2026-07-20) — same rule: vendor binaries AND their
# verbatim extracted-text twins stay LOCAL (a full-text dump is the vendor's
# words, not our summary). The committed record is external/ServiceNow/README.md
# (the SOURCE-MANIFEST) + knowledge/upgrade-plans/servicenow-cmdb-analysis.md.
external/ServiceNow/*.pdf
external/ServiceNow/*.pptx
external/ServiceNow/*.docx
external/ServiceNow/extracted/

# External-vendor documentation CAPTURES (scripts/external_vendor_scrape.py) —
# the ServiceNow rule generalized: a verbatim scrape of a vendor help tree is
# the vendor's copyrighted words, not our summary, so it never enters a repo
# that is private-but-sometimes-published. The real landing zone is OUT of the
# tree entirely (DRYDOCS_DATA_ROOT/vendor-docs/<capture-id>/, per
# drydocs_core.data_root.vendor_docs_dir) — these patterns are belt-and-braces
# for anyone who mirrors a capture in-tree. What IS committed: the capture id
# and its doc-source-registry entry, and whatever summaries we write ourselves
# under external/orchestration/.
external/vendor-docs/
vendor-docs/
**/capture-manifest.json

# Design-doc PDFs (Epic L / L4) — BUILD-ON-DEMAND from the .md via scripts/doc_to_pdf.py.
# The .md is the source of truth and the single .html render is committed (L13); the PDF is a
# regenerable binary (not byte-identical run-to-run — trailer /ID varies), so it is not tracked.
# Regenerate before printing for the pen/paper loop.
docs/design/*.pdf

# Paper-HITL scans (Epic L / L6) — raw scanned/photographed annotated printouts. Internal
# by default (see docs/design/feedback/scans/README.md + config/classification.yaml
# excluded_paths): never published unless a human deliberately reclassifies. Keep the
# README (the classification note) tracked; the raw scans are not.
docs/design/feedback/scans/*
!docs/design/feedback/scans/README.md

# Editor workspace settings (machine-local)
/.vscode/

# Scratch screenshots dropped at the repo ROOT (review finding F10, 2026-07-25).
# Working screenshots — Neo4j browser captures, SQL logs, UI states — accumulate here
# during a session and are never referenced by anything. Root only: deliberate image
# assets live in docs/design/ui-exploration/, drydocs-icons/, internal/pat-evidence/ and stay tracked.
# Nothing tracked matches this (verified at the time it was added).
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# derived mapping-store materialization (plan M0) - rebuild via scripts/build_mapping_db.py
var/
